edule my own stuff  for later you know  um so a lot of freelance is just keeping  your schedule in its rains and stuff  changes constantly it drives me crazy  um yeah I don't think it's like I need  to  totally choose ever I try to make time  for everything  um  but you know like in my work like  for a feature or whatever if I have two  weeks to shoot or whatever over X period  of months like I can find those days  that are always working around whatever  other work I have because I'm the one  planning those so I can decide when they  are uh so I don't think it's a choice so  much but yeah there always needs to be  some work coming in  was that part of your plan to always  have some time for your own projects for  the two of you yeah I mean I know that  they say like hey if you get a job in  reality TV you might make great money  but then it may be harder to get your  own stuff made because you're so bound  with these schedules yeah  um yeah definitely somebody was asking  me recently if I wanted to go into  reality I'm like I don't know that I  want to work every day for six months  you know like because I need my down  time and physically like you know I'm  not the youngest anymore like there's  definitely a reason why you know a lot  of backbreaking work happens in your 20s  you know I'm getting a little bit older  and I don't want to be that like  damaging to my back and stuff like you  know carrying camera every day for  months and months and months like I can  do it for two weeks fine you do it for a  month fine but like when that there's no  end in sight no break in sight I don't  know if that's for me that's why I like  features where it's like you got a month  you got two months easy you take a break  you know  um  so yeah  I think it is always important for me to  have my own thing going because I need  to have control over something  in my life so I need to be the one like  you know if something's not right it's  my fault and that's fine and I can  accept that uh but at least like I am  the person trying the hardest you know  um  and then like you know you can go off  and work on whatever but you know I  always need something that's mine that's  cooking you know Brewing yeah because  some people make that decision early in  life or then sometimes maybe after they  have a successful corporate career you  know what I need time to do creative  stuff and that's the most important  thing over making money and I get it  when you have kids you can't make that  decision but  yeah I wasn't sure if maybe being  available to have projects or being able  to do whatever you want  was more of a  decision maker in what jobs you take oh  yeah um certainly yeah like for me it's  all about  um you know like that's why I like being  a director for photography because it is  creative you know and I do have a lot of  say in the project as a whole  um but other jobs and stuff that's just  filling in my schedule and I do it  because I've learned the skills you know  these are the skills I have now so I  might as well let them make me a little  bit money on this side you know but yeah  it's always about my own stuff that's  like what's the goal is I guess you know  is to be doing myself on a bigger and  bigger level my own projects uh and  everything else is is feeding into that  machine for me career-wise you know  um but yeah that's certainly the most  important thing always is the art and  what I'm doing  um but I have a lot of fun you know like  I like being an AC like I said like I  have a lot of fun doing it if the set's  good and the people are fun you know and  you're doing good work that's good  enough for me for that period of time  you know I can put the other stuff aside  for a month or two months or whatever  um but yeah there always needs to be  something that I'm working on in the  back burner
 

